Bug: the generator yields the same mutable list object (`window`) repeatedly; since that list is mutated after each yield, all previously yielded items appear to change. Fix: yield an immutable snapshot (tuple) each time, and handle the case where the iterable is shorter than n.

Fixed version:

def sliding_window(iterable, n):
    it = iter(iterable)
    window = []
    try:
        for _ in range(n):
            window.append(next(it))
    except StopIteration:
        raise ValueError('iterable too short')
    yield tuple(window)
    for x in it:
        window.pop(0)
        window.append(x)
        yield tuple(window)
